      "subject": "article"
    },
    {
      "detail": "SI page 8 calls the precursor 3. The drawn cyclic product, lactam reduction and reported precursor mass/mmol identify 4 (365.5 g/mol), not acyclic 3 (393.6 g/mol). This is an explicit interpretation pending review.",
      "id": "precursor2",
      "severity": "source_conflict",
      "subject": "E05"
    },
    {
      "detail": "SI page 9 calls the starting compound 13, also the product label. The reported starting mass/mmol matches secondary amine 3; N,N-dimethyl quaternization is represented as 3 to 13, pending review.",
      "id": "precursor13",
      "severity": "source_conflict",
      "subject": "E06"
    },
    {
      "detail": "SI page 6 draws formic acid beside 4 but prints C24H33N3O2. Parent plus one formic acid would contain O3. The route uses the covalent parent with adduct metadata, without assigning a protonation site or corrected isolated formula.",
      "id": "salt4",
      "severity": "source_conflict",
      "subject": "4"
    },
    {
      "detail": "SI page 10 HRMS formula C16H24N disagrees with drawing C15H23N and m/z 218.1903, which match protonated C15H24N. Both source and graph-derived formulas are retained.",
      "id": "formula17",
      "severity": "source_conflict",
      "subject": "17"
    },
    {
      "detail": "SI labels neutral formulas C13H27NO2 and C21H31NO as [M+H]+. The reported masses match their protonated ions. Neutral formulas are not treated as ion formulas.",
      "id": "ion-formula",
      "severity": "source_notation",
      "subject": "6/15"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Reported yield is 23%; the amount of amine 17 is absent. Yield is transcribed, not recomputed from the separately given acid amount.",
      "id": "yield15",
      "severity": "source_incompleteness",
      "subject": "E08"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Wavy tetrahedral bonds remain unspecified; 4 is an E/Z 7:1 mixture. No E/Z ratio is inferred for final 2 from its precursor.",
      "id": "mixtures",
      "severity": "representation_boundary",
      "subject": "2/3/4/13"
    },
    {
      "detail": "SI page 7 describes Boc derivatization of crude RCM material for LC-MS ratios, including a repeat-unit dimer drawing. These analytical derivatives are outside the preparative target and control routes.",
      "id": "analytical-boc",
      "severity": "representation_boundary",
      "subject": "10/11/12"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The source reports the acetal-to-tetrahydro-beta-carboline preparation as one event; no unreported aldehyde intermediate is invented.",
